    {
      "text": "Figure 2(a): the first blueprint produced for multivariate Taylor's theorem in integral form, before any automated proving. Rectangles are definitions and ellipses are theorems; dashed arrows mark a statement-level use and solid arrows a proof-level use. Definition nodes taylorKernel, taylorRemainderKernel, taylorPoly, lineMap and lineCurve sit at the top; the target frechet_taylor_integral is the sink at the bottom. Most theorem nodes are light blue (unproved); only taylor_integral_one_shot, integrationByParts_smul and ftoc_bochner_wrapper are dark green.",
      "state": "draft",
